# Budget Tracker

An interactive Budget Tracker web application built using HTML5 and CSS3 as part of the Web Development module.

## Features Implemented

### 1. Structured Data Table
- Utilizes semantic HTML table tags: `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tbody>`, `<tr>`, `<th>`, and `<td>`[span_0](start_span)[span_0](end_span).
- Displays expense logs cleanly with columns for Date, Category, Description, and Amount[span_1](start_span)[span_1](end_span).

### 2. Enhanced Expense Entry Form
- Standard `<form>` element wrapping all inputs[span_2](start_span)[span_2](end_span).
- Includes a `<select>` dropdown menu with 5 categories (Groceries, Utilities, Entertainment, Transportation, Healthcare)[span_3](start_span)[span_3](end_span).
- Proper input-label linkage using matching `for` and `id` attributes[span_4](start_span)[span_4](end_span).
- Form submission triggered via a `<button type="submit">` element[span_5](start_span)[span_5](end_span).

### 3. Multimedia Components
- `<img>` element with descriptive `alt`, `src`, `width`, and `height` attributes[span_6](start_span)[span_6](end_span).
- `<iframe>` embedding external educational content with proper `src`, `title`, and dimension attributes[span_7](start_span)[span_7](end_span).

### 4. Advanced CSS Styling
- `:nth-child(even)` pseudo-class selector for zebra-striped table rows[span_8](start_span)[span_8](end_span).
- Attribute selector (`button[type="submit"]`) to style interaction controls[span_9](start_span)[span_9](end_span).
- Direct child combinator (`section > h2`) to target section subheadings[span_10](start_span)[span_10](end_span).
